      "side": 1,
      "message": "Further notes:\nI was able to observe the original performance regression on my machine pretty easily, and the SkAnySubclass version appears to restore the baseline performance, so that\u0027s good.\n\nThere is some wonkiness with the factories (and some extra work happening, I think) - to keep the outer class unaware of the derived ones, I had to use a templated constructor [1]. You can\u0027t specify the type explicitly when calling a templated constructor, so I did the obvious thing that works - always passing an instance of the actual derived object, to then be copy-constructed into the container [2]. This pattern has to be reflected up to the factories themselves [3]. The alternative to was have the factories use a constructor that doesn\u0027t initialize the backend data at all, then manually/explicitly fill it out -- I didn\u0027t like having a constructor that leaves them half initialized, so I went with the current approach. \n\n[1] https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/738882/12/include/gpu/GrBackendSurface.h#184\n[2] https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/738882/12/include/gpu/GrBackendSurface.h#187\n[3] https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/738882/12/src/gpu/ganesh/GrBackendSurfacePriv.h#92",
